# The profile SVGs are generated artifacts (scripts/generate.py). The daily CI
# workflow regenerates and commits them, which otherwise collides with locally
# regenerated copies on every pull/rebase. The custom "regen-svg" merge driver
# resolves any such conflict by re-running the generator, so the merged result
# is always a fresh, source-consistent SVG instead of a manual conflict.
#
# The driver must be registered once per clone (it lives in .git/config, which
# is not shared). Run scripts/setup-merge-driver.sh — or:
#   git config merge.regen-svg.name "regenerate profile SVGs"
#   git config merge.regen-svg.driver "python scripts/generate.py && cp %P %A"
assets/*.svg merge=regen-svg
